<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55450" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατατυγχάνω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hit one's mark, reach the object of</i> . . ,
				[<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ἐλπίδος</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Demad.
				6
			</span></i>,cf. <i><span class="en">
				Diocl.Fr.
				138
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς στρατείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					13.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς σπουδῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					3.25
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> abs., <i>to
				be lucky</i> or <i>successful</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαμαρτάνω</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.178
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν θέσιν εὔχεσθαι δεῖ
				κατατυγχάνειν</span> as to the situation of the city, one
			must hope <i>to be successful</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1330a37
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c. dat.,
				<i>fall to the lot of</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Procop.
				<u>Arc.</u>
				4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, in abs. sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Euryph.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.39.27
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to be in office at the time</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ κ. ἀρτυτήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Test.Epict.</u>
					4.37
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(3).249.36
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Anaphe</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
